  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A deep analysis of what the AI development ecosystem is actually building in 2026 — and what's conspicuously absent from existing coverage",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Introduction: The Map Is Not the Territory",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "If you've been following the AI development space in 2026, you've seen the narratives: vibe coding is revolutionizing software, coding agents like Claude Code and Codex are replacing developers, and local-first AI is the path to sovereignty",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "These narratives are real",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "update frequencies, and comparing what people are *actually building* versus what they're *writing about* — is that there exists a complete, functional stack for AI-native full-stack development that is largely invisible to existing coverage",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "2. \"Which coding agent is best",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "These are the wrong questions. The right question — the one the actual ecosystem is answering — is : **\"What is the complete stack for building software with AI agents, and how do all the pieces fit together",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "This post maps that stack. It identifies the blind spots in existing coverage. And it explains why context engineering — not vibe coding, not coding agents, not local models — is the actual paradigm shift",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Before I identify the blind spots, let me establish what the ecosystem is actually doing",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The existence of this many agents is itself a signal: no single agent wins",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "This is the single most important development that existing coverage is missing",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "An **agent harness** is the layer between the AI model and the tools it uses",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Context Engineering](https://github.com/coleam00/context-engineering-intro) (13.5K stars, updated daily) represents a fundamental reframing:",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Context Engineering is 10x better than prompt engineering and 100x better than vibe coding",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Session capture** — Every action, decision, and output is recorded",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "CC Switch](https://github.com/farion1231/cc-switch) (112K stars) is a cross-platform desktop all-in-one assistant for Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, OpenClaw, Gemini CLI, and Hermes Agent",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "The existence of this tool signals something important: developers are using multiple agents simultaneously, and they need a way to manage them",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Now let me identify what's missing. I've analyzed the blog's existing 136 posts, the broader AI development coverage, and the actual ecosystem. Here are the blind spots:",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "2.1 Blind Spot #1: Context Engineering Is the Paradigm, Not Vibe Coding",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Vibe coding works for prototypes. It breaks down at scale because the context window is finite",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Context engineering solves this by treating context as a first-class artifact — something you design, structure, and maintain. The template is a complete system for providing comprehensive context: documentation, examples, rules, patterns, and validation",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Why this matters:** The shift from vibe coding to context engineering is the shift from \"asking the AI nicely\" to \"giving the AI everything it needs to succeed",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "2.2 Blind Spot #2: The Agent Harness Is the Real Operating System",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "An agent harness is what sits between the model and the tools",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Why this matters:** Without a harness, your coding agent is just a model with a terminal",
      "confidence": null,
      "evidence_refs": []
    }
  ],
